{"name":"Ironclad","hex":"#615c55","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ironclad","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Covered with iron, steel, or  any other tough metal; armor-plated.","Solid or certain; not able to be disputed or questioned; irrefutable."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ship, vessel, or vehicle with a covering of iron, steel, or  any other tough metal.","An armor-plated warship,  one preceding the invention of harveyized steel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ironclad"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ironclad (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Ironclad is a 2011 British action historical drama film directed by Jonathan English. Written by English and Erick Kastel, based on a screenplay by Stephen McDool, the cast includes James Purefoy, Brian Cox, Kate Mara, Paul Giamatti, Vladimir Kulich, Mackenzie Crook, Jason Flemyng, Derek Jacobi, and Charles Dance. The film chronicles the siege of Rochester Castle by King John in 1215. The film was shot entirely in Wales in 2009 and produced on a budget of $25 million."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/36/Ironclad_%282011_movie_poster%29.jpg/330px-Ironclad_%282011_movie_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ironclad_(film)","wikidata":"Q1150930"},{"title":"Ironclad (software)","blocks":[{"text":"Ironclad is a software as a service company that makes contract management software. Founded in 2014 and headquartered in San Francisco, California, Ironclad provides a platform for legal and business teams to create, store, and manage contracts online in a process known as contract lifecycle management."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ironclad_(software)","wikidata":"Q122363621"},{"title":"Ironclad warship","blocks":[{"text":"An ironclad was a steam-propelled warship protected by steel or iron armor constructed from 1859 to the early 1890s. The ironclad was developed as a result of the vulnerability of wooden warships to explosive and incendiary shells. The first ironclad battleship, Gloire, was launched by the French Navy in November 1859, narrowly preempting the British Royal Navy. However, Britain built the first completely iron-hulled warships."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/HMS_warriorjune20092.jpg/330px-HMS_warriorjune20092.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ironclad_warship","wikidata":"Q1410980"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/36/Ironclad_%282011_movie_poster%29.jpg/330px-Ironclad_%282011_movie_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/36/Ironclad_%282011_movie_poster%29.jpg/330px-Ironclad_%282011_movie_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIronclad.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Rochester_Castle%2C_Kent_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1582414.jpg/500px-Rochester_Castle%2C_Kent_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1582414.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Rochester_Castle%2C_Kent_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1582414.jpg/500px-Rochester_Castle%2C_Kent_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1582414.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rochester Castle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARochester_Castle%2C_Kent_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1582414.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/James_Purefoy_and_Jamie_Foreman%2C_Rochester_Castle.jpg/500px-James_Purefoy_and_Jamie_Foreman%2C_Rochester_Castle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wi